From: econet-42x6 port <local>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: airoha: exclude the TX_DISABLE pad from the EN7523 "pon" group

The EN7523 "pon" pin group as introduced together with the SoC support
lists pins 28..33, i.e. GPIO16..GPIO21.  Pin 28 is GPIO16, which on the
EcoNet vGP-42X6V1 (and on the EN751221 reference design) is the
board-level TX_DISABLE line of the optical frontend and is therefore
consumed as a *GPIO* by the xPON PHY driver:

    priv->tx_disable_gpio =
        devm_gpiod_get(dev, "tx-disable", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);   /* not optional */

Applying the "pon" mux state claims every pin of the group through
pin_request(), so the GPIO request for that very same pad is refused:

    pinctrl-airoha-en7523 ...: pin gpio16 already requested by 1faf0000.phy;
                               cannot claim for 1fbf0200.system-controller:pinctrl:528
    pinctrl-airoha-en7523 ...: error -EINVAL: pin-28 (...:pinctrl:528)
    airoha-xpon-phy 1faf0000.phy: error -EINVAL: failed to get TX disable GPIO
    airoha-xpon-phy 1faf0000.phy: probe with driver airoha-xpon-phy failed with error -22

which leaves the whole xPON stack unprobed (/sys/class/xpon empty, OMCI
commands returning -ENODEV).

Drop pin 28 from the group so that the PON-owned pads are muxed while
GPIO16 keeps its split ownership, exactly as described in
phy-airoha-xpon.c:

    "PON pad routing belongs to pinctrl.  In particular GPIO16 is the
     board-level TX_DISABLE line on the EN751221 reference design while
     GPIO17..20 remain owned by the PON hardware."

This mirrors the downstream fix (930-264: pon_pins { 16..20 } -> { 29..33 }).
The PON_MODE register bit written by airoha_pinmux_set_mux() is unchanged.

--- a/drivers/pinctrl/airoha/pinctrl-en7523.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/airoha/pinctrl-en7523.c
@@ -330,7 +330,7 @@
 	PINCTRL_PIN(41, "pcie_reset1"),
 };
 
-static const int pon_pins[] = { 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33 };
+static const int pon_pins[] = { 29, 30, 31, 32, 33 };
 static const int pon_tod_1pps_pins[] = { 21 };
 static const int gsw_tod_1pps_pins[] = { 21 };
 static const int sipo_pins[] = { 13, 38 };
